{
  "id": "ep032",
  "duration": 46.516,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.813,
      "text": "Our galaxy is falling toward an invisible cosmic monster.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.8,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.813,
      "end": 8.158,
      "text": "We are hurtling through the dark at 1.3 million miles per hour.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Map of voids in the CosmicFlows-3 volume of the Local Universe.jpg",
        "credit": "H. M. Courtois, R. van de Weygaert, M. Aubert, D. Pomar\u00e8de, D. Guinet, J. Dom\u00ednguez-G\u00f3mez, E. Florido, L. Galbany, R. Garc\u00eda-Benito, J. M. van der Hulst, K. Kreckel, R. E. Miura, I. P\u00e9rez, S. Planelle",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_voids_in_the_CosmicFlows-3_volume_of_the_Local_Universe.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.8,
          "end": 8.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 8.158,
      "end": 14.178,
      "text": "For decades, the thick gas and dust of the Milky Way completely blocked our view of this giant.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Majestic Milky Way (milkywaylasilla-cc).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO/F. Char",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Majestic_Milky_Way_(milkywaylasilla-cc).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 8.167,
          "end": 10.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 10.767,
          "end": 14.167,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.178,
      "end": 21.173,
      "text": "In the 1980s, astronomers used infrared and X-ray telescopes to finally pierce this barrier.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "CSIRO ScienceImage 4350 CSIROs Parkes Radio Telescope with moon in the background.jpg",
        "credit": "division, CSIRO",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CSIRO_ScienceImage_4350_CSIROs_Parkes_Radio_Telescope_with_moon_in_the_background.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.167,
          "end": 16.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 16.833,
          "end": 21.167,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.173,
      "end": 28.068,
      "text": "They discovered the Great Attractor, a gravitational basin holding around 100,000 galaxies.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "View Towards the Great Attractor.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_Towards_the_Great_Attractor.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.167,
          "end": 25.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.7,
          "end": 28.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.068,
      "end": 34.388,
      "text": "But astronomers quickly realized this region has far too little mass to cause such a violent pull.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "View Towards the Great Attractor.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_Towards_the_Great_Attractor.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.067,
          "end": 34.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.388,
      "end": 40.863,
      "text": "Instead, a much larger titan called the Shapley Supercluster is dragging the entire region.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "More Galaxies of the Shapley Supercluster (28330672719).png",
        "credit": "geckzilla",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:More_Galaxies_of_the_Shapley_Supercluster_(28330672719).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.4,
          "end": 36.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 36.867,
          "end": 40.867,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.863,
      "end": 46.166,
      "text": "Cosmic expansion will eventually pull us away, but for now, we continue our plunge.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.867,
          "end": 46.5,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
